BEFORE15 = mean separation over [onset-15, onset-1] in local sd.
DURING   = [onset, onset+30].   AFTER = [onset+31, onset+60].
class    = which window holds the LARGEST POSITIVE separation;
           'none(+)' means no window is positive on average.
epochs+  = onsets where BEFORE15 > 0, out of those covered.

Only a BEFORE classification can support advance warning. A DURING
classification is contemporaneous detection, however large.

